3.2.4.5 CAP PDU Prediction Service

The CAP PDU Prediction Service is an advanced Machine Learning and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) microservice that provides intelligent analytics, predictive capabilities, and natural language querying for DIS simulation data. It is a Python/Flask application that leverages state-of-the-art ML models including transformers, vector embeddings, and similarity search to deliver AI-powered insights and conversational interfaces for data exploration and analysis. The service integrates with processed PDU data from PostgreSQL and other platform services to provide comprehensive ML-driven predictions and intelligent data interpretation.

## Service Overview

The CAP PDU Prediction Service is a Python/Flask microservice that manages:
- Advanced ML-powered predictive analytics for DIS PDU data using scikit-learn
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system for natural language queries
- Vector embeddings and similarity search using sentence-transformers and FAISS
- Conversational AI interfaces for intelligent data exploration
- Integration with Kong Gateway for HTTP endpoint security
- Real-time data integration with Data Acquisition Service
- Health monitoring and observability endpoints

## Architecture Integration

### Kong Gateway Integration
- Public endpoints: /api/prediction/health, /api/prediction/chat/status (health monitoring)
- Protected endpoints: /api/prediction/chat, /api/prediction/* (ML services with Firebase JWT authentication)
- Automatic JWT validation at Kong Gateway level for protected endpoints
- CORS and rate limiting policies applied at gateway level
- User context forwarding via headers for personalized ML responses

### Data Integration
- PostgreSQL read access via Data Acquisition Service for historical PDU analysis
- Real-time metrics integration with Data Ingestion Service
- HTTP-based service-to-service communication with JWT authentication
- Data caching mechanisms for performance optimization (2-second cache duration)
- Vector store integration for similarity search and retrieval

### ML/AI Architecture
- Transformer-based models: Google FLAN-T5-small for natural language generation
- Sentence embeddings: all-MiniLM-L6-v2 for semantic similarity and retrieval
- Vector database: FAISS for efficient similarity search and clustering
- Linear regression models: scikit-learn for time-series prediction
- GPU/CPU optimization: Automatic device selection for optimal performance

